    { "id": "db-shard-title", "type": "text",
      "x": 1022, "y": 170, "width": 214, "height": 18,
      "text": "Sharding  (when needed)",
      "fontSize": 13, "fontFamily": 1, "textAlign": "center", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "roundness": null, "seed": 51, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 51,
      "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1, "link": null, "locked": false
    },
    { "id": "db-shard-detail", "type": "text",
      "x": 1022, "y": 194, "width": 214, "height": 505,
      "text": "When primary can't\nhandle write throughput\n\nWhat: split data\nacross multiple DB\ninstances (shards)\n\nStrategies:\n\n1. By user_id\n   user_id % 3\n   → Shard 0,1,2\n\n2. By geography\n   US users → Shard A\n   EU users → Shard B\n\n3. By tenant (SaaS)\n   CustomerA → Shard 1\n   CustomerB → Shard 2\n\nEach shard:\n→ its own primary\n→ its own replicas\n\n⚠️ Tradeoffs:\n• No cross-shard JOINs\n• App must know which\n  shard to query\n• Rebalancing is hard\n• More operational cost\n\n→ Use replicas first!\n  Shard only when\n  writes are the\n  bottleneck",
      "fontSize": 9, "fontFamily": 1, "textAlign": "center", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#555", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "roundness": null, "seed": 52, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 52,
      "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1, "link": null, "locked": false
    },

